[low, perf/memory] gix-store — the Rc<Schema> cache (store.rs:117-125) is both bypassed and unbounded. Bypassed: migrate.rs steps_from (migrate.rs:103) calls Schema::read_pinned directly for every history hop, so each get_migrated of a value bound k schemas back re-reads and re-decodes k full schema documents from the ODB with no reuse across calls; Kind::decode (kind.rs:114) and current_schema (kind.rs:548) likewise skip the cache. Routing these through Store::schema(tree) is a one-line change each. Unbounded: the HashMap grows for every distinct schema tree ever read; fine for a CLI process, worth a note (or a cap) for the long-running library consumers gix-store is positioned for (query/effect daemons).
